  displayName: "Cha Cha Cha"
  style: 2
  origin: "Cuba"
  history: "Cha Cha Cha was created in Cuba in the early 1950s, when violinist and composer Enrique Jorrin wrote music with a new, catchy rhythm. The name copies the sound of the dancers' feet on the quick triple step: cha-cha-cha. It is playful, cheeky and very precise."
  timeSignature: "4/4"
  tempoMinBarsPerMinute: 30
  tempoMaxBarsPerMinute: 32
  difficulty: 2
  characteristics:
  - "Playful and flirty"
  - "Sharp and rhythmic"
  - "Counted 2, 3, 4-and-1"
  skills:
  - "Cuban motion (hip action)"
  - "Fast, neat footwork"
  - "Straight leg action"
  - "Precise timing"
